From: Mohammed Naser <mnaser@vexxhost.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [libvirt] Render hook scripts with the chart context

The hook scripts were rendered with "tpl $v .", where "." is the script
string inside the range loop. Helm 3 requires the second argument of
tpl to be the chart values and fails with:

  wrong type for value; expected chartutil.Values; got string

Pass $envAll instead. Scripts can now reference .Values and .Release.

Drop this patch once the chart is bumped to a release that includes
the fix.
---
diff --git a/libvirt/templates/configmap-bin.yaml b/libvirt/templates/configmap-bin.yaml
index 0ff74c9..bf0ab50 100644
--- a/libvirt/templates/configmap-bin.yaml
+++ b/libvirt/templates/configmap-bin.yaml
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ data:
 {{- if .Values.conf.hooks.enabled }}
 {{- range $k, $v := .Values.conf.hooks.scripts }}
   {{ $k }}: |
-{{ tpl $v . | indent 4 }}
+{{ tpl $v $envAll | indent 4 }}
 {{- end }}
 {{- end }}
 {{- end }}
